From 210d55e2ec4e70693b41218bb1a7b4c943d9b51b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:39:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: WDT time-out, window mode and early warning (U2251)

The watchdog counts CLK_WDT_OSC, 1.024 kHz, with the timings of a
PIC32CM MC00 measured by firmware/hello APP=wdtprobe: CTRLA changes
synchronize for 3 to 4 clocks and CLEAR for 2 to 3, by the write's
phase, with SYNCBUSY meanwhile; the count starts one clock before an
enable completes and restarts when a CLEAR completes; early warning
after EWOFFSET clocks (only below PER) or at the start of the open
window; the reset after PER or WINDOW + PER clocks. A wrong CLEAR key
resets when its sync completes, also while the WDT is disabled (one
clock later), and so does a clear in the closed window. Reserved PER,
WINDOW and EWOFFSET values count as 16384 clocks, as PER 0xC did on
silicon. ALWAYSON now survives system resets and leaves WEN writable.

Resets come from a timer, so they no longer wait for the CPU to leave
the access that asked for them. qtest pic32cm-wdt-test; the JH01
reset-cause test steps past the CLEAR sync.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
